<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#caravel">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caravel</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A caravel was a small, highly manoeuvrable sailing ship developed by the Portuguese in the fifteenth century, often with lateen sails that allowed it to sail close to the wind. It was used in voyages of exploration along the African coast. The caravel was a key tool of the early maritime expansion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>.</p></div>
